# Run to create (needs the YubiKey master identity):
#   agenix-rekey edit ./dmvault-secrets.age
#
# Contents (KEY=value format) — five keys:
#   DATOMIC_PASSWORD=<alphanumeric only. It is embedded in DATOMIC_URL below,
#                     and non-URL-safe chars (; ! / + # & space) break parsing.
#                     Generate a safe one with `openssl rand -hex 24`.>
#   ADMIN_PASSWORD=<datomic admin password — MUST differ from DATOMIC_PASSWORD>
#   DATOMIC_URL=datomic:free://datomic:4334/orcpub?password=<DATOMIC_PASSWORD>
#   SIGNATURE=<random 20+ char string; symbols are fine (never used in a URI)>
#   EMAIL_SECRET_KEY=<Resend API key, starts with re_>
#
# orcpub reads DATOMIC_URL verbatim and does NOT append a password, so the
# transactor's `datomic` storage password MUST be embedded in the URL. The
# password therefore appears twice (DATOMIC_PASSWORD and inside DATOMIC_URL) and
# the two MUST be identical — the transactor inits H2 storage with the former,
# the app authenticates to it with the latter. A mismatch (or a missing
# `?password=`) is H2 "Wrong user name or password [28000-171]".
#
# Rotating the password on an EXISTING store is not just an edit here: H2 keeps
# the old credential on disk. Either wipe /storage/data/dmvault/data/* and let
# the transactor re-init, or set ADMIN_PASSWORD_OLD/DATOMIC_PASSWORD_OLD on the
# datomic container for one start so it rotates the stored credential.
